      "text": "Consider the angle triangle $\\angle$ CBF and using the given information, we can apply the law of sines to get:\n$$\\frac{FB}{\\cos{30^\\circ}} = \\frac{AC}{\\cos{60^\\circ}}$$\n$$FB = AC \\frac{\\cos 30^\\circ}{\\cos 60^\\circ}$$\n$$FB = AC \\frac{\\sqrt{3}/2}{1/2}$$\n$$FB = AC\\sqrt{3}$$\nApplying the law of cosines with sides AC and FB, we get\n$$1^2 = AC^2 + FB^2 - 2 \\cdot AC \\cdot FB \\cdot \\cos{120^\\circ}$$\n$$1 = AC^2 + (\\sqrt{3}AC)^2 - 2AC \\cdot \\sqrt{3}AC \\cdot (-1/2)$$\n$$1 = AC^2 + 3AC^2 + AC^2\\sqrt{3}$$\n$$1 = 4AC^2 + AC^2\\sqrt{3}$$\n$$1 = AC^2(4 + \\sqrt{3})$$\n$$AC^2 = \\frac{1}{4 + \\sqrt{3}}$$\nNow I will take the positive square root (why bother taking the negative?) and I can simplify my fraction.\n$$AC^2 = \\frac{(4 - \\sqrt{3})}{(4 - \\sqrt{3})(4 + \\sqrt{3})}$$\n$$AC^2 = \\frac{4 - \\sqrt{3}}{16 - 3}$$\n$$AC^2 = \\frac{4 - \\sqrt{3}}{13}$$\nNow dealing with the length using my formula above, I can simplify it too.\n$$OB^2 = AC^2 + FB^2 - 2 \\cdot AC \\cdot FB \\cdot \\cos{180^\\circ}$$\n$$OB^2 = \\frac{4 - \\sqrt{3}}{13} + 3(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})^2 -2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{4 - \\sqrt{3}}{13}$$\n$$OB^2 = \\frac{4 - \\sqrt{3}}{13} + 3(\\frac{3}{4}) - 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{4 - \\sqrt{3}}{13}$$\n$$OB^2 = \\frac{4 - \\sqrt{3}}{13} + \\frac{9}{4} - \\frac{2(\\sqrt{3})^2 - 2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 4}{13}$$\n$$OB^2 = \\frac{4 - \\sqrt{3}}{13} + \\frac{9}{4} - \\frac{12 - 2\\sqrt{3}}{13}$$\n$$OB^2 = \\frac{(4 - \\sqrt{3})}{13} + \\frac{87}{52} - \\frac{(12 - 2\\sqrt{3})}{13}$$\n$$OB^2 = \\frac{4 - \\sqrt{3}}{13} + \\frac{87 - 52(2\\sqrt{3})}{52}$$\n$$OB^2 = \\frac{4 - \\sqrt{3} + 87 - 104\\sqrt{3}}{52}$$\n$$OB^2 = \\frac{91 - 107\\sqrt{3}}{52}$$\nFinally, $OB^2 = \\frac{91 - 107\\sqrt{3}}{52}$\n$$OB^2 = \\frac{91 - 107\\sqrt{3}}{52} = \\frac{1}{13} (\\frac{91}{4} - \\frac{107\\sqrt{3}}{1})$$\nAs the maximum length is always positive, I only care about the value of the positive square root\n$$OB = \\sqrt{\\frac{91 - 107\\sqrt{3}}{52}}$$\n$$OB \\approx 0.99615$$",
